WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.251
In news that I am sure will come as a shock
to absolutely no one who's been [inaudible]

00:00:05.251 --> 00:00:06.251
paying attention.

00:00:06.251 --> 00:00:10.309
The Senate is set to acquit Donald Trump in
his impeachment trial.

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:14.700
By the time you listen to today's show, by
the time you watch this segment, it may already

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.700
have happened.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.700
It may be soon to happen.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.789
It may be a happening tomorrow.

00:00:18.789 --> 00:00:21.220
Now, let me do something here.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:25.429
If you've not been following the situation
in the Senate and I actually over the weekend,

00:00:25.429 --> 00:00:27.369
I talked to some friends who said, I haven't
seen anything.

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:28.490
I said, you're better off.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:33.720
Quite frankly, you might wonder, why is it
not shocking that Trump is going to be found

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.620
not guilty in his impeachment trial?

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:41.081
Well, if you've not been following the trial,
you might think that this is a trial, like

00:00:41.081 --> 00:00:46.719
a normal trial where the the jurors, the 100
senators in the Senate will come in with an

00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:48.109
open mind.

00:00:48.109 --> 00:00:55.289
They will hear the evidence, they will welcome
evidence and then they will evaluate the facts

00:00:55.289 --> 00:01:01.000
to decide whether an impeachment conviction
of Donald Trump makes sense or otherwise,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.089
whether an acquittal of Donald Trump makes
sense.

00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:08.160
That's what you might think if you had not
been paying attention at all, in which case

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.060
I envy you, but that's not the situation we
have.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:16.920
We knew in advance that because there are
53 Republican senators in the Senate and you

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:22.990
need 67 senators to vote to convict in order
to get a conviction in an impeachment trial

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:28.329
in the Senate, Republicans had made it clear
they plan to acquit in advance.

00:01:28.329 --> 00:01:33.170
We knew that Trump was going to be found not
guilty no matter what happened.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:39.760
Now, unfortunately, it's even worse because
it's not just that Republican senators decided

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.700
in advance that they were going to equip Donald
Trump, but they went through and at least

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.290
pretended to be handling this like a normal
trial.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:49.010
It's worse than that.

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:56.250
Republicans voted on Friday not to even hear
from witnesses firsthand witnesses while claiming

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.549
for months.

00:01:57.549 --> 00:02:00.719
The problem is we don't have any firsthand
witnesses here.

00:02:00.719 --> 00:02:05.700
And this is why the term cover up is increasingly
being used to describe, describe what is a

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:06.979
sham impeachment trial.

00:02:06.979 --> 00:02:11.880
Now Republicans have been using the term sham,
not a sham, like a sham.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:12.880
Wow.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:16.320
The type you would use, you know, a terrycloth,
uh, a dish towel that you would use to clean

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:17.320
things.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.700
They've been using the term sham to describe
the mere fact that Donald Trump was impeached

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.020
by the house.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.640
And of course it's often projection.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:29.460
There was a sham here, but the sham was that
this was anything like a real trial.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.790
And in a way, I know I've said before and
a lot of people don't like when I say this,

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:39.230
that Mitch McConnell has been an extremely
asset to Republicans and one of the most effective

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:40.230
Republican, uh, tools.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:46.400
And I say that not, not in, in the, um, a
pejorative way, but a very useful tool to

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.400
Republicans.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.100
You've got to hand it to them.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:54.560
Republicans have played this really, really
well at the start of the trial, Democrats

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.380
wanted to decide, are we going to have witnesses?

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.380
Are we going to have documents?

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.690
Are we going to issue subpoenas?

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:03.230
And Republicans said, let's figure that out
later.

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:05.810
Of course Republicans had the majority, so
they got it.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:09.360
Republicans successfully said, let's do 64
hours of trial.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:15.240
First, 24 hours of house, impeachment managers,
24 hours of Trump's attorneys, 16 hours of

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:16.330
Senator questions.

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:20.930
Let's do all of that first and then we will
decide about witnesses and every time that

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:26.240
Democrats stood up and said, I have an amendment
for the proceedings where we will decide now

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:27.240
about witnesses.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.780
Republican said, we already have a plan for
that.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:34.780
We're going to do that after 64 hours of proceedings
in any other trial, it would not have been

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:35.980
done this way.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:41.860
In any other trial, you decide first about
witnesses and evidence so that both sides

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:46.680
can build their cases around the witnesses
and the documents.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:52.020
That would be part of the trial, but Republicans
control the Senate and they got their way.

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:57.210
And then we saw last week, we talked about
this during my live streams as the 64 hours

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:00.480
of proceedings, we're starting to reach the
end.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:05.330
Republicans started to slip in this line that
we noticed, which is once we're done with

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:13.290
these 64 hours, we'll decide whether we really
need to hear more, and this is evil genius

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:18.360
because they started making it about have
we had enough hours of trial when really the

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:22.330
issue is not, do we need 64 or 84 104 hours
of trial?

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:27.060
The issue is, are there material firsthand
witnesses who could testify and the answer

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:28.060
is yes.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:33.120
Former national security advisor, John Bolton,
remember Republican said, nobody here is a

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:34.160
firsthand witness.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.160
It was a lie.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.740
Binman was a firsthand witness.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:40.800
We had others, but John Bolton would unquestionably
be a firsthand witness.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:41.800
They don't want them.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:45.960
Bolton saying in his upcoming book and likely
would say the same thing under oath, which

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:51.600
is Donald Trump personally told me, hold the
aid to Ukraine until they publicly smear Joe

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:52.600
Biden.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:53.600
That's a firsthand witness.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:54.600
They don't want it.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.590
Rudy's henchman love Parness.

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:58.590
He has recordings.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:04:59.590
He is not.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:02.760
We have a, by the way, a second video in which
he is meeting with Donald Trump.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.940
He was putting physical surveillance on ambassador
Maria Vonnegut.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.660
She's a firsthand participant.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.870
Now we don't need to hear him.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:15.040
Republicans say the acquittal means nothing,
but it also means everything to the people

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:19.320
who just want to be let off the hook so they
can vote for Trump in November of 2020.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:24.530
If you complain about no firsthand witnesses
and simultaneously blocked firsthand witnesses,

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:26.130
you are not an honest actor.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.830
You are not a good faith participant.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:31.110
So let's just cut to the end of the story
because I think most of you know where this

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:32.110
